    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0133" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg124"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/833: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-07T15:00:00+01:00">June 7, 1940—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 7—1:16 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>481. My 465, June 5, 3 p.m., and 459, June 4, 11 a.m.<anchor n="90"
                        xml:id="d155-f1"/> In reply to my inquiry this morning Ciano informed me
                    definitely that the <hi rendition="#italic">Rex</hi> would not sail and added
                    that I had been right in recommending that the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washington</hi> should not plan to enter the Mediterranean.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d155-f1" n="90" xml:id="d155-f1-content">
